#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: sunless sea.
#> pause: 50
#> must: In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
#> must: A stately pleasure dome decree:
#> must: Down to a sunless sea.
#> not: Where Alph
#> not: measureless
#> source: /ran\nThrough/d
# 16. P and D: a sliding two-line window. McMahon 3.4
# P prints up to the first newline; D deletes up to it and restarts the script
# without reading a new line if something is left. With $!N; P; D each cycle
# holds a line and the one after it. The address /ran\nThrough/ only matches
# when "ran" ends one line and "Through" starts the next: those two lines, as
# a pair, are deleted. Lines 1, 2 and 5 pass through the window one at a time.
# Try: change d to s/\n/ ... / and the pair is joined instead of deleted.
$!N
/ran\nThrough/d
P
D

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
A stately pleasure dome decree:
Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
Through caverns measureless to man
Down to a sunless sea.
